\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Fitted class mean trajectories $\alpha _k + \beta _k a + \gamma _k a^2$ (with $a = (\text  {age}-55)/10$) for the state-space specification at three and four classes. Rows: the physical GRM as P-FULL (\texttt  {\small  theta\_phys\_full}, functioning plus diagnosis groups) and as P-FUNC (\texttt  {\small  theta\_phys\_func}, functioning only), each standardised over its fitted sample. Columns: K=3 and K=4, fitted to the same people. Line width is proportional to the class share; class 1 is worst health. The strip beneath each panel is the class composition of the person-waves observed at each age.}}{34}{figure.11}\protected@file@percent }
